    {
      "skoolId": "5e6032ba7a44475483ecc3fad62b1645",
      "content": "This guys background is crazy\n\nGuy Gu’rari, Co-Founder of Augment an AI-powered platform for software development that provides services for chat, code completions, and guided edits. Former Google research scientist who was instrumental in helping move the company from solely using vision models pushing whats possible with generative language models shortly after the launch of OpenAI’s GPT3 in May of 2020.\n\nMasters and PhD graduate in physics from the Weizmann Institute of Science, Postdoctoral Fellow at Stanford University, and Member of Princeton’s Institute for Advanced Study (also known as the IAS - a home to early giants like Albert Einstein and Oppenheimer).\n\nThat’s over a decade of studying topics spanning string theory, high energy theoretical physics and machine learning. Guy’s names been cited over 15k times in various research papers according to Google Scholar. Guy went all in on Machine learning while at the IAS and pitched Google on bringing a group of his team members on to help the company.",
      "createdAt": 1750794634138,
      "updatedAt": 1750794634138,
      "authorEmail": "me@parkerrex.com",
      "postSkoolId": "165b2f0aba554469ab872382eb53d903",
